From: Pavel Snajdr <snajpa@snajpa.net>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kpatch-build: skip objects that cannot be reconciled on 6.12.95

Two objects in the 6.12.95 vpsadminos build cannot be processed by
create-diff-object:

  - kernel/trace/ring_buffer.o: the changed functions of the accepted
    ring-buffer row (6d666f0b8b36, recreated as bc8f306b) have no
    patchable function entries in the boot vmlinux - their prologues are
    plain "push %rbp; mov %rsp,%rbp" where a patchable function starts
    with "call __fentry__" (contrast the carried
    __x64_sys_perf_event_open).  The row is carried boot-only with the
    native 6.12.110 ancestry, not by the online 6.12.95 payload.
  - drivers/net/ethernet/chelsio/cxgb4/t4_hw.o: a faithful two-sided
    rebuild shows identical code, rodata, relocation and symbol tables;
    only debug line-number data differs.  Zero changed functions.

Both objects contribute no patchable content to this module; skip them
the same way usr/initramfs_data.o is skipped.

Signed-off-by: Pavel Snajdr <snajpa@snajpa.net>
---
 kpatch-build/kpatch-build | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/kpatch-build/kpatch-build
+++ b/kpatch-build/kpatch-build
@@ -1445,6 +1445,11 @@
 		[[ "$i" = arch/x86/lib/copy_user_64.o ]] && continue
 
 	[[ "$i" = usr/initramfs_data.o ]] && continue
+	# Objects that create-diff-object cannot reconcile on the 6.12.95
+	# base and that contribute no patchable functions to this module;
+	# ring_buffer.o's row is carried boot-only, t4_hw.o is debug-only.
+	[[ "$i" = kernel/trace/ring_buffer.o ]] && continue
+	[[ "$i" = drivers/net/ethernet/chelsio/cxgb4/t4_hw.o ]] && continue
 
 	mkdir -p "output/$(dirname "$i")"
 	cd "$BUILDDIR" || die
